  "note": "Election of 21 members for the three wards of Omagh Urban District, due 18 May 1949. There were no contests: nominations closed on 4 May and 'the 12 candidates selected by the Unionist Party and the nine candidates chosen by the Nationalist Party were returned unopposed' (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3; also Londonderry Sentinel, 5 May 1949, p. 5). New members named for this ward by the Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3: John Cadden. The retiring members (Robt. Rodgers, W. J. Hamilton, A. T. Blair, J. Hammond, S. S. Wilson) are filed in the ward by inference: division inferred from the 18 September 1946 return; the Ulster Herald, 30 April 1949, p. 5 and the Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3 name the member as returned. All sat on the new council's committees (Ulster Herald, 28 May 1949, p. 5). The paper prints no labels per candidate. Returned unopposed."
